Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='versionnotcompiled', at=datetime(2026, 10, 13, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The version is no compiled input: the binary reads app/release.toml at run time', body="THE VERSION IS NO COMPILED INPUT (2026-10-13, with the selective gate): `app/Cargo.toml`'s version is fixed at 0.0.0, no crate's source reads `app/release.toml` (guards' `a_release_cut_changes_no_file_a_crate_compiles`), and the binary reads it at RUN TIME (2026-10-14): `.#suzatary-bin` is built without it, and `.#suzatary` copies that binary beside `share/suzatary/release.toml`, which `suzatary_cli::stamp::release` reads from beside the executable (for `/api/about`, `--version`, `doctor`; the package runs `--version` before it ships), so a train moves no gate key and compiles no binary (`scripts/release-free.sh`, a gate step, evaluates both derivations with another release); a cargo build says `dev`. A version the tree declares that no tag names (the hand-set 1.10.0) folds into the next release. Never set the version or close `## [Unreleased]` by hand. The flake reads the release file for the APK's name. The contracts keep their own snapshots (`app/core/tests/mcp-surface.json`, the stored vocabulary under `app/core/tests/`), so widening one fails a test instead of drifting.", rationale='Decided 2026-10-13 with the selective gate; read at run time since 2026-10-14.', supersedes=()))